          "label": "Instructions",
          "type": "string",
          "nullable": false,
          "blank": "reject",
          "unit": "text"
        }
      ],
      "referenceData": [
        {
          "topic": "Scope",
          "instructions": "The configured employees, service positions and four complete repair proposals. Change availability, payroll or comparison priority here; a different restaurant roster needs an adapted author profile."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Starting values",
          "instructions": "Prefilled values are fictional examples. Changing part of the workbook can leave example inputs in the case."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Editing",
          "instructions": "Edit the named input sheets. Keep worksheet names, column headers and record identifiers. Do not add formulas. Other case inputs remain unchanged."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Units and time",
          "instructions": "Relief availability uses HH:mm on Saturday, America/Chicago. Other intervals remain elapsed minutes from 2026-11-16T00:00:00-06:00. Payroll limit uses dollars; employee pay rates retain the explicitly labelled canonical units."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Import",
          "instructions": "Upload this workbook, inspect the changes and diagnostics, then apply. Importing does not calculate results or establish operating permission."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Relief cook availability",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. The complete working interval for Rowan on Saturday. An early finish does not shorten the required service."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Remaining payroll limit",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Complete remaining payroll in USD dollars, including retained assignments and the repair. The import converts dollars to canonical cents. Additional expense is calculated against the retained baseline."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Comparison priority",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Choose an authored priority. Every mandatory staffing and expense requirement remains unchanged. Compare without ranking leaves every passing repair available."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Employee work records",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Only authored employee identities are supported. Fees are flat amounts per assignment. Earlier work is retained as minutes and the latest previous shift end."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Recorded qualifications",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Recorded qualifications for the authored roles. A missing qualification cannot establish suitability for that role."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Complete proposed repairs",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Complete assignments to every authored position. Changing the employee, position or proposal catalog requires authoring a new profile and publishing a new version."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Other working availability",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Working intervals for the other employees, with breaks and unavailable periods omitted. The relief cook interval is supplied separately."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Other employee commitments",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Existing overlapping work using the same employee identities and week clock. Empty means no other commitments are recorded for this comparison."
        }
      ]
    },
